  { q: 'How many photos can fit in a 100KB PDF?', a: 'For clear, readable document pages, aim for about 30–50KB per page, so two or three photos. More pages are possible but text gets harder to read.' },
  { q: 'Should I choose A4 or Fit image?', a: 'A4 is safest for forms because officers may print it. Fit image avoids white borders and is fine for on-screen viewing.' },
  { q: 'My photo comes out sideways. What do I do?', a: 'PDFSherpa reads your camera’s rotation data automatically. If a photo is still sideways, the camera didn’t save that data. Fix it afterwards with <a href="/rotate-pdf">Rotate PDF</a>.' },
